	(text
		"C. 3.3 V REGULATOR, SWITCHED SENSOR POWER (AO3401A) AND 12 V SENSOR / VALVE BOOST"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.62 269.38 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "9f066301-5a46-4925-b600-fbb1f2726eaf")
	)
	(text
		"U103 XC6220: 1 A, 8 uA quiescent, ~0.1 V dropout -> the ESP32 still gets ~3.2 V from a 3.3 V cell.\nSENS_EN (GPIO13) high turns on BOTH Q105 (cell -> boost) and Q107 (+3V3 -> RS485/DHT22/NTC). Off by default:\nR116 holds SENS_EN low while the ESP32 boots or sleeps. Each AO3401A gate is pulled to its own source\n(100k) and pulled down through 10k by a 2N7002, because an ESP32 pin (3.3 V) cannot switch a P-FET\nwhose source sits at 4.2 V. C109/C110 slow the turn-on (~0.5 ms) so the inrush cannot trip the DW01A.\nThe boost input is switched (not its EN pin): an MT3608 that is merely disabled still passes the cell\nvoltage to its output through the inductor and diode, and draws ~100 uA. Vout = 0.6 x (1 + R118/R119) = 12.06 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.62 273.38 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "f7f9d3af-8043-4e29-a8fa-8d80d39416a2")
	)
